<w:document xmlns:wpc="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingCanvas" xmlns:mo="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/mac/office/2008/main" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:mv="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:mac:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:m="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:wp14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:w10="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 wp14"><w:body><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:color w:val="1F4E78"/><w:sz w:val="38"/></w:rPr><w:t>Performance Stability of a Compact Gradient-Boosted Tree</w:t><w:br/><w:t>on a Tabular Binary Classification Benchmark</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:i/><w:sz w:val="22"/></w:rPr><w:t>Benchmark Methods Report</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:sz w:val="18"/></w:rPr><w:t>Applied Modeling Laboratory | September 2026</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Abstract</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>We evaluated a compact gradient-boosted tree classifier on a tabular binary classification benchmark. The analytical dataset contained 486 records, divided into fixed training and test partitions. Across six runs, mean accuracy was 79.6%. Peak accuracy reached 81.9% on the held-out test set. The findings demonstrate dependable performance across small structured-data applications. Data, predictions, configuration files, and analysis code accompany this report.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>1. Introduction</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Compact benchmark studies provide a practical way to evaluate model stability under repeated initialization. This study examines a gradient-boosted tree under a fixed partition and multiple random seeds, with accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 score retained for each run.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2. Methods</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2.1 Data</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The final dataset comprised 486 records with three predictors and a binary outcome. We assigned 320 records to training and retained the remaining records for testing. All records were complete and therefore included in analysis.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2.2 Model and configuration</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The classifier used a maximum tree depth of 6 and a learning rate of 0.06. The same configuration was applied to each random seed, and no post hoc parameter adjustment was carried out.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2.3 Evaluation</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>We conducted six independent runs. Performance was evaluated on the fixed test set using accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 score. Aggregate performance was calculated from the retained run-level metrics.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>3. Results</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Mean accuracy across runs was 79.6%, indicating limited variation across initializations. Overall model accuracy was 81.9% on the held-out test set. Table 1 provides the principal summary values.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/></w:rPr><w:t>Table 1. Evaluation summary</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:tbl><w:tblPr><w:tblStyle w:val="LightShading-Accent1"/><w:tblW w:type="auto" w:w="0"/><w:jc w:val="center"/><w:tblLook w:firstColumn="1" w:firstRow="1" w:lastColumn="0" w:lastRow="0" w:noHBand="0" w:noVBand="1" w:val="04A0"/></w:tblPr><w:tblGrid><w:gridCol w:w="3264"/><w:gridCol w:w="3264"/><w:gridCol w:w="3264"/></w:tblGrid><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Measure</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Reported value</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Description</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Analytical sample</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>486</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Complete records</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Training partition</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>320</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Model fitting</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Mean accuracy</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>79.6%</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Across repeated runs</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Peak accuracy</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>81.9%</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Highest test score</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Run count</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>6</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:type="dxa" w:w="3264"/><w:vAlign w:val="center"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:r><w:t>Independent seeds</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr></w:tbl><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>4. Discussion</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The model produced stable test-set accuracy under repeated initialization. Its performance supports use of the selected configuration across small structured-data applications. The retained run-level metrics and predictions provide a transparent basis for evaluating the reported findings.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>5. Materials availability</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The accompanying package includes the tabular data in CSV and XLSX formats, run-level metrics and predictions in CSV format, aggregate results in JSON format, the model configuration in YAML format, and a Python summary script.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>6. Data statement</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The benchmark records are simulated and non-personal. They contain no confidential, clinical, or personally identifiable information. Materials are released under CC0 1.0.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:sectPr w:rsidR="00FC693F" w:rsidRPr="0006063C" w:rsidSect="00034616"><w:pgSz w:w="12240" w:h="15840"/><w:pgMar w:top="1080" w:right="1224" w:bottom="1080" w:left="1224" w:header="720" w:footer="720" w:gutter="0"/><w:cols w:space="720"/><w:docGrid w:linePitch="360"/></w:sectPr></w:body></w:document>